# Reverse-engineering workspace. The extracted Obsidian/Mermaid payloads are
# proprietary (Obsidian is License: UNLICENSED, Vendor: Dynalist Inc.) and
# Corbomite is GPLv3, so no part of the corpus may be committed -- not the
# minified bundle, not the readable/renamed tree, not the rename map.
#
# The *tooling* is ours and is the reproducibility story: it regenerates the
# whole corpus from the .deb. That is deliberate -- the previous audit's corpus
# was a renamed tree at a path that no longer existed with no surviving name
# map, which is why its symbol citations are now unverifiable. Don't repeat
# that: if you move or delete RE/tools, the corpus becomes unreproducible.
RE/*
!RE/tools/
RE/tools/node_modules/
